Subject: [PATCH] Show background terminal transcript hints

Base: openai/codex rust-v0.159.2
ff6aec96948b70d94983af2641a6b67c94faeff5

Keep completed and replayed background-terminal snapshots consistent with
the Ctrl+T hint that command_display_lines displays. Preserve retained output
and exploration group boundaries.

TDD snapshot receipts:
- cargo +1.95.0 test -p codex-tui --lib chatwidget::tests::exec_flow
  -- --test-threads=1
  RED in the combined patch queue: 58 passed, 2 failed. The adjacent
  exploration and unified-exec-unknown snapshots omit the completed command's
  literal (ctrl+t to view transcript) hint.
  GREEN after updating those two snapshots: 60 passed using the compiled
  combined-queue test executable identified by Cargo's run receipt.
- cargo +1.95.0 test -p codex-tui --lib exec_cell: 23 passed in the queue,
  including completed_background_terminal_includes_transcript_hint.

Checks use RUST_MIN_STACK=16777216 and remove inherited WT_SESSION, TERM,
and COLORTERM for the upstream noninteractive snapshot environment.
